---
/**
 * Global background, adapted from the shadcnblocks background-pattern117
 * block (`npx shadcn add @shadcnblocks/background-pattern117`) — a "matrix"
 * dot grid (tiny 1px dots on a 3px pitch, tinted with the theme's primary
 * color) faded out via a radial mask. Only the background layer itself was
 * kept — the block ships a full demo hero section (badge, heading, buttons)
 * that this site has no use for, so that placeholder content was discarded
 * rather than committed unused.
 *
 * Rebuilt as static markup rather than importing the React component: it's
 * purely decorative with no interactivity, so there's no reason to ship a
 * client bundle for it. References the shadcn theme bridge's --primary
 * token directly, so it re-colors automatically in dark mode.
 *
 * The same dot pattern (--dot-grid-matrix-bg in global.css) is reused by
 * the footer and the client-logo marquee so all three ambient surfaces
 * match instead of mixing this grid with the old large-dot one.
 *
 * Fixed (not absolute) so it reads as one wallpaper behind the whole page
 * rather than a pattern that scrolls away after the first screen.
 *
 * No z-index (relies on being first in the DOM, so later siblings simply
 * paint over it): a NEGATIVE z-index here — the original `-z-10` — breaks
 * `backdrop-filter: blur()` for every descendant elsewhere on the page
 * (the header's frosted-glass nav pill and mega-menu panel). Confirmed by
 * isolated repro: a backdrop-filter element can't blur a sibling painted
 * via negative z-index, but blurs the exact same sibling fine once it's
 * just behind in normal (non-negative) stacking order. This element is
 * already first in the DOM and everything else on the page paints after
 * it, so dropping the negative z-index costs nothing and fixes the blur.
 */
---

<div
  class="fixed inset-0 pointer-events-none bg-dot-grid-matrix"
  style="mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 95% 54% at 50% 100%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45) 0%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2) 34%, transparent 74%); -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 95% 54% at 50% 100%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45) 0%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2) 34%, transparent 74%);"
  aria-hidden="true"
>
</div>
